\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED - OFFICIAL-Yuan should be added to SDR basket -Mundell\b0\par\par\uc2 474 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2009\par 13:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Robert Mundell corrects his suggestions in 5th paragraph for new SDR \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weightings and includes latest SDR weightings. His previous suggestions were based on out-of-date SDR weightings)\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, April 7 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan should be added to the basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that underpin the IMF's special drawing right next year, as a step toward creation of a global reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nobel Prize laureate and architect of the euro Robert Mundell said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 He endorsed Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Zhou Xiaochuan's call last month for the U.S. dollar to be replaced as the world's main reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the IMF's Special Drawing Right (SDR) [ID:nPEK184558], and said volatile exchange rates had helped cause the global financial crisis last September.\par \par \uc2 "It's time for a change. The Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> is now the third most important \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world ... arguably more important than the (Japanese) yen, depending on how you measure it," Mundell told a news conference in Hong Kong. "I believe that in 2010, the yuan should be added to the SDR."\par \par \uc2 The Columbia University professor won the Nobel Prize for Economics in 1999 and is often credited as the intellectual father of the euro for his research on optimal \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  zones.\par \par \uc2 The IMF's SDR is reviewed every five years and the next review is due late next year. Mundell suggested reducing the dollar's SDR weighting to 40 percent, from 44 percent; keeping the euro weighting at 34 percent; reducing the Japanese yen's <JPY=> 11 percent weighting to 10 percent, and cutting the pound sterling's <GBP=> 11 percent weighting to 8 percent. The yuan would take up the remaining 8 percent, he said, even though it is not fully convertible.\par \par \uc2 The strength of the yuan excess demand, which is pushing the yuan higher and forcing \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and buy foreign reserves to keep it in check would compensate for the lack of convertibility, he added.\par \par \uc2 Under Mundell's view of an international monetary system based on a global reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than the U.S. dollar, the yuan's convertibility is not such an important issue so long as the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains loosely aligned to the U.S. dollar, he said.\par \par \uc2 Gold could also be included in the SDR basket to help hedge against inflation, he said.\par \par \uc2 An aide to the Russian government on Tuesday urged the International Monetary Fund to publish a study on prospects for a new international reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Susan Fenton, Editing by Kazunori Takada) (susan.fenton@thomsonreuters.com; +852 2843 6367; Reuters Messaging: susan.fenton.thomsonreuters.com@reuters.net)\par \par \uc2 FINANCIAL-SDR/MUNDELL (CORRECTED)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|ABX|BNX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090408e548000qw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
