\par\par \b \uc2 Taiwan dollar at one-week high on China comments\b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 02:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Taiwan dollar at one-week high\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  optimism, US$ profit-taking\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited (Adds details, quotes)\par \par \uc2 TAIPEI, March 5 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> firmed sharply on Thursday as China's comments on relations with Taiwan and economic growth helped boost the island's financial markets.\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar firmed 0.6 percent to as high as T$34.830 to the U.S. dollar, the strongest level since Feb. 26. By 0250 GMT, it had erased some gains, but still traded higher at T$34.960 from the previous close of T$35.067.\par \par \uc2 Volume on the main \uc2 Taipei \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Inc\uc2  exchange was moderate at $431 million after an hour and 45 minutes of trade.\par \par \uc2 "The market is banking on hopes of China's economy," said a dealer in Taipei. "Some investors, including foreign banks, who had long positions in the U.S. dollar think it is a good time to take profits."\par \par \uc2 China's Premier Wen Jiabao assured that the country will achieve 8 percent growth this year despite a deepening financial crisis, which helped boost market sentiment in Asia.\par \par \uc2 Wen also said China was ready to talk peace with Taiwan, a move that the island's government welcomed, in increasing signs of easing tensions between the political rivals.\par \par \uc2 Taiwan's shares <.TWII> rose 1.53 percent on the news, after rising as much as 3 percent in earlier trade.\par \par \uc2 "We've already seen some foreign fund inflows in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said the first dealer.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought some U.S. dollars in the market to try and stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid for U.S. dollars, but it wasn't particularly active. I think it doesn't really want to go against the overall trend of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a second dealer said.\par \par \uc2 On the smaller Cosmos exchange <COSMOS1>, the Taiwan dollar strengthened to T$34.965 to the U.S. dollar from the previous close of T$35.052. (Reporting by Lee Chyen Yee and Rachel Lee, Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-TAIWAN-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|Z|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090308e5350000s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
