\par\par \b \uc2 DJ US Says Reform,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Marked  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  Exchange-Rate Regime\b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2008\par 22:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2008, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--A Treasury Department report says gradual reform and heavy government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  characterized \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exchange rate regime.\par \par \uc2 Treasury on Wednesday released a report to Congress on International Economic and Exchange Rate Policies.\par \par \uc2 In the report, Treasury said it hasn't found that any major trading partner of the U.S. met the standards as identified in the Omnibus Trade and Competitiveness Act of 1988 during the first half of 2008.\par \par \uc2 The law says the Treasury secretary will analyze the exchange-rate policies of foreign countries. It says the secretary will consider whether countries manipulate the rate of exchange between their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. dollar for purposes of preventing effective balance of payments adjustments or gaining unfair competitive advantage in international trade.\par \par \uc2 The report that said in the first half of 2008, Chinese authorities allowed greater flexibility in the dollar exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 It also said China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  engaged in record levels of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Gradual reform and heavy government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue to characterize \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's managed float exchange rate regime," according to the report.\par \par \uc2 That regime is officially described as a managed float with reference to a basket of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of China's major trading partners.\par \par \uc2 The report said the renminbi gained 6.2% against the dollar in the first half of 2008. -By Jeff Bater, Dow Jones Newswires; 202-862-9249; jeff.bater@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2008 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020081210e4ca00b9l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
