\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan falls to lower limit of daily band vs dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 175 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 2008\par 10:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Dec 1 (Reuters) - The yuan fell sharply on Monday, hitting the lower limit of its daily trading band against the dollar, as dealers speculated China might adjust its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, permitting more yuan weakness, to stimulate its slowing economy.\par \par \uc2 It was the first time that the yuan had touched the bottom of its trading band since its peg to the dollar was abolished in July 2005.\par \par \uc2 The Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <CNY=CFXS> tumbled as far as 6.8848 to the dollar. It is permitted to fluctuate 0.5 percent on either side of the day's mid-point <CNY=SAEC>, which the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set on Monday at 6.8505.\par \par \uc2 Traders said they did not see significant \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yuan by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Lu Jianxin; Editing by Andrew Torchia)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN-LIMIT (URGENT)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|Z|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|O|OIL|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081204e4c10013a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
