\par\par \b \uc2 China says at IMF that yuan closer to fundamentals\b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2008\par 19:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, Oct 13 (Reuters) - China said on Monday that improvements in the country's balance of payments showed that greater \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility had already moved its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closer to an appropriate market-set level.\par \par \uc2 "Exchange rate flexibility has increased markedly and the exchange rate increasingly reflects the fundamentals," said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Yi Gang in a statement to the board of governors of the International Monetary Fund.\par \par \uc2 Yi wash echoing comments he made at the IMF on Saturday concerning the yuan, also known as the renminbi, but added more details of how Beijing views recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been under pressure for years to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold down the value of the yuan against the euro and dollar to boost exports. Yi noted the growth of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves had slowed and the trade surplus had narrowed.\par \par \uc2 "In the past two months, the renminbi has appreciated 15 percent against the euro. The ongoing improvement in China's balance of payments demonstrates that the renminbi exchange rate is closer to the fundamentals," Yi said.\par \par \uc2 Drawing a stark comparison with the troubles of a global credit crisis centered in the United States and Europe, Yi stressed that his own country was in much better shape.\par \par \uc2 "Financial institutions in China remain sound. After several years of comprehensive financial reforms, the capital adequacy of financial institutions has reached a historical high," he said, adding that market liquidity was "ample". (Reporting by Alister Bull; editing by Neil Stempleman)\par \par \uc2 CHINA-IMF/|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|Z|UKI|CANT|J|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081013e4ad001qm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
