\highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  helped to stabilise the spot market once again by setting a nearly flat reference rate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nSHA134599]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China stocks tumble 3.6 pct but banks off lows\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SHANGHAI - The Chinese stock market fell sharply on Friday because of the crash of global share prices, but China outperformed Asia as banking stocks came well off early lows on hopes for government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nSHA161604]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bond yields plunge on money market freeze\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SHANGHAI - Medium- and long-term Chinese government bond yields plunged on Friday, posting their biggest daily drops in years, as a continued freezing up of interbank lending diverted money into bonds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nSHA351717]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China bond yields fall on 3-year auction result\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SHANGHAI - Chinese bond yields fell on Friday in response to a very strong auction of three-year government bonds, traders said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nSHA28615]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** Money market freeze behind strong China bond sale\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SHANGHAI - China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold bonds on Friday at a yield that was much lower than expected, but traders said the auction was strong partly because a freezing up of the interbank money market was driving money into bonds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nSHA153283]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLICY NEWS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China will refund bank reserve cut in yuan -paper\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING - China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will return in yuan the cash freed up by this week's cut in reserve requirements, even though it has obliged banks to lodge dollars to meet increases in required reserves over the past year, an official newspaper said on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nPEK20727]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China halts IPOs to help stock market -paper\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HONG KONG - China's stock market regulator has effectively suspended initial public offerings to tighten the supply of equity and strengthen its stock market amid the global financial crisis, a newspaper reported on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nHKG168606]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China aims to boost domestic demand\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING - China will make forceful efforts to boost domestic demand and promote balance in its international payments, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nBJC000211]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ECONOMIC NEWS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** Chinese business confidence weakens sharply in Q3\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING - China's business confidence index fell sharply in the third quarter to 123.8 points, down from 134.8 in the second, the official Xinhua news agency said on Friday, citing figures from the National Bureau of Statistics.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nPEK103082]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China soybean imports to remain strong -survey\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING - China's purchases of soybeans are expected to remain strong in the weeks ahead as lower shipping prices help spur deals by the world's largest buyer, a survey by an official think-tank showed on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nPEK174608]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China Jan-Sept FDI rises 39.9 pct on year earlier\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING - China drew $74.37 billion in foreign direct investment (FDI) in the first nine months of 2008, 39.9 percent more than a year earlier, the Commerce Ministry said on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nBJB000501]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China to grow 10.1 pct in 2008 - govt think-tank\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING - China's economy will grow 10.1 percent in 2008 and 9.5 percent in 2009 despite the crisis engulfing global markets, the government's top think-tank said in a report released on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nPEK161006]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China car sales fall for 2nd month as economy ebbs\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SHANGHAI - China's passenger car sales shrank for a second month in a row in September, official data showed on Friday, as a slowing economy slammed the brakes on fast-growing demand in the world's second-largest vehicle market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nSHA173041]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CORPORATE NEWS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China '08 coke exports to drop by 15-20 pct -assn\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING - China's coke exports are likely to fall to between 12 million and 13 million tonnes in 2008, a drop of 15 percent to 20 percent from the year before, the head of an industry association said on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nPEK158687]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 To see a guide on contributions, please click <CN/CONT1>. (Compiling by Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Edmund Klamann) (Shanghai newsroom, +86 21 6104-1688, fax +86 21 6104-1728, shanghai.newsroom@reuters.com))\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|Table|Z|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LB