\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Taiwan dlr jumps, Singapore dlr capped by c.bank   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kevin Yao   \par \uc2 775 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2008\par 04:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Feb 25 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar hit a new high on Monday after the island's politicians pledged to boost direct flights with \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stalled gains in the Singapore dollar, despite strong inflation.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were shackled in narrow ranges, mirroring regional stocks <0#.INDEXA>.   \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> hit a fresh 2-1/2-year high at 31.25 per U.S. dollar, up 0.8 percent from Friday's close, buoyed by a promise from the island's presidential candidates during a weekend debate to step up direct flights with China.   \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar has gained around 3.3 percent since the opposition KMT party's landslide win in legislative elections last month, which raised expectations that its candidate, Ma Ying-jeou, will win the presidential elections in March.   \par \par \uc2 That would help reduce cross-straits tensions and spur the island's economy, but some analysts believe prospects of rising inflation would support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the longer term.   \par \par \uc2 "The Taiwan dollar's strength, led by the recent strong portfolio inflows, could serve as an extra channel for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tackle inflationary pressure more effectively," Goldman Sach analyst Enoch Fung said in a note.   \par \par \uc2 The bank raised its forecast on the Taiwan dollar, expecting the unit to hit 30.75, 30.5 and 30.25 in 3, 6 and 12 months, respectively, up from 32, 32 and 31.5 previously.   \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=> briefly rose to 946.2 per dollar as local shares rose, but analysts said foreign investors were selling local stocks and that would support the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 C.BANK CAPS SINGAPORE DOLLAR   \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> pulled back to 1.4060 per U.S. dollar after briefly hitting an 11-year high of 1.4050 as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of buying U.S. dollars, but analysts expect the Singapore unit to rise to help curb inflation.   \par \par \uc2 "They have been there since last week, but all they can do is slow the pace of the U.S. dollar's decline," said a trader.   \par \par \uc2 A second dealer agreed: "I reckon they will try to prevent spot falling below 1.4050."   \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise past the psychologically important 1.40 level in the near future.   \par \par \uc2 Consumer prices in January rose 6.6 percent from a year earlier, the fastest pace since 1982, government data showed on Monday. [ID:nSGC001786] [SGCPIY=ECI]   \par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> eased slightly to 7.15 per dollar, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped in offshore non-deliverable forwards <CNYNDFOR=>, pricing in more than 10 percent gains in 12 months.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the pace of appreciation to gain steam again after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it would step up use of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help rebalance the economy.   \par \par \uc2 "We are likely to see the continued appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a pace of around 8-10 percent this year and the next," analysts at  \uc2 UBS\uc2  said in a note.   \par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  has forecast a 12 percent rise in a year.   \par \par \uc2 The yuan has gained a further 13.5 percent since it was revalued in July 2005, including by 2.2 percent so far this year.   \par \par \uc2 Philippine financial markets are closed for a holiday. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at  0812 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.46         107.29       -0.16\par  Sing dlr        1.4053         1.4063       +0.07\par  Taiwan dlr      31.250         31.495       +0.78\par  Korean won      947.00         948.40       +0.15\par  Baht             32.28          32.32       +0.12\par  Rupiah         9125.00        9170.00       +0.49\par  Rupee            40.01          40.05       +0.11\par  Ringgit         3.2145         3.2160       +0.05\par  Yuan            7.1495         7.1418       -0.11\par  Change so far in 2008\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.46         111.33       +3.60\par  Sing dlr        1.4053         1.4382       +2.34\par  Taiwan dlr      31.250         32.443       +3.82\par  Korean won      947.00         935.70       -1.19\par  Baht             32.28          33.68       +4.34\par  Peso             40.60          41.28       +1.67\par  Rupiah         9125.00        9390.00       +2.90\par  Rupee            40.01          39.41       -1.49\par  Ringgit         3.2145         3.3050       +2.82\par  Yuan            7.1495         7.3041       +2.16\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by Jacqueline Wong)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080228e42p0007p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
