\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan eases on global dollar rise, uptrend intact   \b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2008\par 06:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Jan 10 (Reuters) - The yuan slipped against the dollar on Thursday, propelled by the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength on global markets, but dealers said the yuan should soon resume its recent uptrend.   Before trading began, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set its daily mid-point <CNY=SAEC> at 7.2805, down from Wednesday's reference rate of 7.2723 as the dollar held its overnight gains against the euro and sterling.   \par \par \uc2  But dealers in the domestic market said they still expected a rapid appreciation of the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term, adding that their expectations had been strengthened after Premier Wen Jiabao warned about inflation this week.   \par \par \uc2  The yuan <CNY=CFXS> was trading at an intraday high of 7.2700 to the dollar at midday, down from 7.2620 at Wednesday's close. If it closes at the midday level on Thursday, it will be the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first daily fall this week.   \par \par \uc2  But the yuan traded far above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's mid-point all morning, hitting an intraday low of 7.2735, suggesting its recent uptrend could resume soon, dealers said. Several dealers predicted the yuan could possibly hit 7.25 next week.   \par \par \uc2  Before Thursday's fall, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used its mid-point to guide the yuan to rise 2.8 percent since late October as it announced in early November that it would use the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a weapon to fight mounting inflation.   \par \par \uc2  "Dealers have been making bets at levels above the mid-point, as the premier's speech suggests China would have to appreciate its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rapidly," said a dealer with a major U.S. bank.   \par \par \uc2  Wen told a cabinet meeting on Wednesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  still faced fairly large inflationary pressures and would temporarily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in goods markets to stabilise prices for basic necessities.   \par \par \uc2  On the offshore market, one-year dollar/yuan non-deliverable forwards <CNY1YNDFOR=> stood at 6.6870/6.6920 in late morning, compared to Wednesday's level of 6.6830/90.   \par \par \uc2  Their latest levels implied yuan appreciation of 8.79-8.88 percent from Thursday's mid-point over the next 12-month period, up slightly from 8.72-8.82 percent the NDFs implied on Wednesday.  (Reporting by Fang Yan; Editing by Anne Marie Roantree)      \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN-MIDDAY|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|Z|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080113e41a0002z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
