\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Faster China  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Gains Favor Asia Over Euro Zone -PIMCO   \b0\par\par\uc2 528 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2007\par 04:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2007, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to appreciate at a faster pace, so investors should be looking at moving money to Asia from Europe, while strong global growth that the Asian giant supports will help lift emerging market assets as a whole, according to PIMCO, the California-based bond fund giant.   \par \par \uc2 'China's own interests are now aligned with an accelerated pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation, and we expect the Chinese yuan to advance at a rate consistent with or exceeding the (annual) 7% implied by the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets today,' wrote Michael Gomez, co-head of PIMCO's emerging markets portfolio management team, in a report published Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 'This argues for shifting exposure away from the Euro Zone, over time, and to Asia, as a stronger yuan clears the way for further advances in non-Japan Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' Gomez said in the report.   \par \par \uc2 'Furthermore, it argues for increasing allocations to emerging-markets assets, as the strong pace of global growth - anchored increasingly by China - should assume a more stable and lasting dynamic as global imbalances unwind,' he said.   \par \par \uc2 China's economy should continue to post strong growth over the long term, supported by 'powerful' urbanization trends alongside relatively low wages, abundant labor and healthy productivity, the report said. 'Threats to China's competitiveness appear to be a long way off,' it added.   \par \par \uc2 The depreciation of the dollar is 'set to continue,' but the euro will not bear so much of this decline in the future as Asian countries will increasingly take up the slack by letting their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate, the report said.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has until now suppressed yuan appreciation with 'massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' to remain competitive, the report said, adding that this is likely to change as the emphasis begins to shift from overseas demand to the domestic market.   \par \par \uc2 'It is becoming increasingly clear that a faster pace of appreciation of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a necessary and appropriate policy response,' Gomez said in the report. And where China goes, other Asian nations follow, he said.   \par \par \uc2 According to PIMCO, a stronger yuan would help address a long list of issues weighing on Chinese policymakers' minds. It would reduce the trade surplus, ease pressure on inflation, mitigate speculative purchases of onshore assets, help the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gain monetary credibility, foster proper allocation of investments, stimulate domestic demand and rebalance the economy.   \par \par \uc2 It would also help disarm protectionist tensions with the U.S. and Europe, he said. The latter is a 'growing concern, given that the E.U. is now China's number-one trading partner and the yuan has significantly depreciated against the euro over the last year,' PIMCO said.   \par \par \uc2 'At the same time, the sterilization costs of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will grow as interest rates in \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise, while those in the U.S. fall,' Gomez said.   \par \par \uc2 'Finally, any concerns of a growth slowdown from the stronger yuan easily could be offset by expansionary fiscal policies, particularly targeted infrastructure and social investment,' he said.   \par \par \uc2 PIMCO web site:   {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.pimco.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.pimco.com  }}}\uc2  -By Matthew Cowley, Dow Jones Newswires; 201 938 5692; matthew.cowley@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -0-    \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020071114e3be001rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
