\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-ECB warns on brutal  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  moves, but is anyone listening?   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Krista Hughes   \par \uc2 1,058 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2007\par 14:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 FRANKFURT, Nov 13 (Reuters) - European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet's caution last week about the perils of "brutal" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements is a warning shot over the heads of investors who have driven the euro to record peaks.   \par \par \uc2 The question is now whether the euro will remain at current levels or take off again, potentially requiring Trichet to fire a second barrel of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or even pull the trigger on the ECB's first \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in seven years.   \par \par \uc2 "If volatility continues to rise we expect the ECB to act again now,"  \uc2 UBS\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Mansoor Mohi-uddin told clients on Monday, recommending they build bets on a softer euro.   \par \par \uc2 Although couched with caution, Trichet's statement was the toughest talk to come out of the ECB on exchange rate movements since 2004 and followed a 3.5 percent rise in the euro-dollar <EUR=> rate in less than two weeks.   \par \par \uc2 In the last two days, a rally and then a pull-back in the yen have taken the focus off the euro, which has eased back from Friday's record high of $1.4753, but analysts said the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could still be vulnerable to fresh upward pressure.   \par \par \uc2 "That's obviated more action from the ECB but that's only because of luck, nothing else," said  \uc2 Morgan Stanley\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Stephen Jen. "Markets have not changed their mind."   \par \par \uc2 Some argue that even an opening salvo has begun a dangerous game of double-bluff with markets, which could end with the ECB losing credibility if it does not follow words with actions.   \par \par \uc2 An added complication is the risk of increased demands from politicians for an interest rate cut to open the interest rate gap with the United States and stem the euro's rise.   \par \par \uc2 Euro-zone finance ministers meeting in Brussels on Monday night made it clear they are unhappy with the strong euro, which threatens to crimp growth already under pressure from continued credit market turbulence.   \par \par \uc2 The head of the BusinessEurope employers' federation, Ernest-Antoine Seilliere, also on Monday called the euro's current level beyond "the threshold of pain" for European companies.   \par \par \uc2 BLUFF GAME BEGUN   \par \par \uc2 In his comments last week, Trichet said "brutal" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were never welcome but did not use that word to directly describe the latest developments, as he did in 2004. Instead, he said recent moves were "undoubtedly sharp and abrupt".   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the form of words was a low-grade warning, albeit a significant one, and could be easily ramped up, perhaps as early as this weekend's Group of 10 central bankers meeting in South Africa.   \par \par \uc2 "That was a soft warning," said Commerzbank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Gavin Friend. "Another 1 or 2 percent in the next few weeks will mark the limits of the ECB's tolerance and we will get a more terse form of words from the ECB."   \par \par \uc2 "I wouldn't expect them to go straight into \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there would have to be some upping of the rhetoric in between."   \par \par \uc2 But the bar for fully-fledged \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is set quite high and a Reuters poll of analysts last week gave only a 20 percent chance of this in the next year. The ECB has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since late 2000, action which followed an 11 percent fall in the trade-weighted euro in 10 months.   \par \par \uc2 So far this year, the euro's value against a basket of major trading \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  <EUREER=ECBF> has risen only 4.5 percent, although to record highs. This contrasts with an 11 percent rise against the dollar, half of it in the last three months.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said it would also be difficult for the ECB to get other central banks on board, as it did in September 2000 with the Bank of Japan and the U.S. Federal Reserve. The ECB has made clear it thinks coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the most effective.   \par \par \uc2 Currently, the dollar's weakness is helping to trim the U.S. trade deficit and any U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would run counter to efforts to persuade \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to free up its exchange rate, a goal shared with the ECB. As for Japan, Japanese Prime Minister Yasuo Fukuda was reported on Tuesday as saying the yen was appreciating too fast, words which proved successful in driving the yen down against the euro as well as the dollar -- hardly action coordinated with the ECB's concerns.   \par \par \uc2 Another hurdle is that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell euros would be at odds with the ECB's warning that it is ready to raise interest rates to head off inflation risks. ECB Executive Board member Lorenzo Bini Smaghi said recently that any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to be consistent with monetary policy.   \par \par \uc2 "This would mean the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to have an easing bias before it considered \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said  \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 's Jen. "Monetary policy is out of sync."   \par \par \uc2 Jen said the market would therefore not take the risk of real \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seriously, a situation which potentially sets the stage for a stand-off between the ECB and the big global funds which traders speculate are behind the dollar's slide.   \par \par \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  economist Gilles Moec said Trichet had embarked on a risky course by showing concern about \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, especially if it failed to prevent a further rise in the euro.   \par \par \uc2 "For a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , revealing its powerlessness is never a good thing," he said.   \par \par \uc2 In 2004, Trichet's use of the word "brutal" came at the news conferences he hosts as chairman of the G10 group of central bankers after regular meetings on the world economy.   \par \par \uc2 Another such opportunity is coming up next Monday in Cape Town, and Moec said if Trichet did want to issue a blunter warning, this would be the logical place.   \par \par \uc2 But will markets care?   \par \par \uc2 "If the market doesn't heed this, or just for a very short period and then attacks again, then you'll know that there's something else underlying this," said Commerzbank's Friend.   \par \par \uc2 "That's what I want to see in terms of whether the market is of a mind to take these guys on."   \par \par \uc2 ECB-EURO/ (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|ABX|BNX|FUN|NAT|UKI|J   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071113e3bd001hr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
