\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Japan  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves rise to record high at end-Aug   \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2007\par 01:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds comments from Yosano, more background)   \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 7 (Reuters) - Japan's foreign reserves, the world's second largest, rose to a record $932.157 billion at the end of August as lower interest rates inflated the value of bonds held in the reserves, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday.   \par \par \uc2  They were up from $923.718 billion at the end of July, rising for the third straight month and marking a record high for the second month in a row.   \par \par \uc2  The reserves at the end of August included $785.602 billion in securities and $125.265 billion in deposits. The rest includes IMF reserve positions, special drawing rights and gold.   \par \par \uc2  Japan's reserves, second only to those of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , ballooned after yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amounting to a record 20 trillion yen ($175 billion) in 2003 and a further 15 trillion yen in the first three months of 2004, as Tokyo tried to keep a rapid rise in the yen from derailing a then-fragile economic recovery and accelerating deflation.   \par \par \uc2  Tokyo has kept out of the market since then, but the reserves have continued to grow steadily, partly on interest rate income.   \par \par \uc2  The government does not disclose the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  breakdown of the external reserves. But historical data on Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has mostly taken the form of dollar buying, suggests most of Tokyo's hefty reserves are in dollars.   \par \par \uc2  Unlike some other countries which have been diversifying their \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves recently, Japan has been reluctant to significantly change the make-up of its reserves, fearing such action could disturb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.   \par \par \uc2  Top government spokesman Kaoru Yosano said on Friday that Japan needs to carefully manage its vast foreign reserves while paying heed to the stability of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.   \par \par \uc2  "If you think about making even a little profit, you would end up with a failure. Sound management will cause few mistakes," Yosano told a news conference.        \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/RESERVES (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070906e3960025h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
