\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-HK banks not at systemic risk from US subprime - HKMA   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Susan Fenton   \par \uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2007\par 10:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details)   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Sept 6 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday that the territory's banks did not appear to face a systemic risk from problems in the U.S. subprime mortgage market but noted there was no room for complacency.   \par \par \uc2 Joseph Yam, chief executive of the HKMA, the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also questioned whether ratings agencies were reacting quickly enough to shifts in market conditions.   \par \par \uc2 "Information submitted by locally incorporated banks to the HKMA indicates that their aggregate exposures to the U.S. subprime mortgage market do not have systemic implications for our banking sector," Yam wrote in a column published on the HKMA's Web site,   {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.info.gov.hk/hkma/eng/viewpt/index.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.info.gov.hk/hkma/eng/viewpt/index.htm  }}}\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 However, he said the outcome of the U.S. subprime mortgage problem and its effect on the global economy were still unpredictable, leaving no room for complacency.   \par \par \uc2 He did not provide any estimates of banks' possible exposure to subprime investments.   \par \par \uc2 Last month,  \uc2 Bank of China\uc2  and its BOC Hong Kong arm reported a combined $11.25 billion in subprime-related holdings.   \par \par \uc2 Local banks have still been affected by the global credit squeeze as interbank rates have headed higher, tracking rises in U.S. interbank rates because Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pegged to the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Three-month interbank rates have edged up in the past few weeks to their highest levels in six years and the three-month interbank rate <HKD3MD=> hit a fresh six-year high on Thursday at 4.87/4.99 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say that is putting more pressure on smaller banks who depend on the interbank market for funding than big lenders such as  \uc2 HSBC\uc2  ,  \uc2 Bank of China (Hong Kong) \uc2 and Standard Chartered Bank .   \par \par \uc2 Liquidity is still strong, however, and the HKMA has not had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, because investor appetite for \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  shares remains firm.   \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong stock market, after sliding last month amid a global equity sell-off on concern about credit risk, has rebounded to record highs since China announced last month that it would allow its citizens to invest directly in Hong Kong stocks soon.   \par \par \uc2 Yam said recent problems faced by global financial institutions reflected wider issues than the U.S. subprime market.   \par \par \uc2 "The experiences of the troubled financial institutions underscore not only the extent of the U.S. subprime mortgage problem but also the risks that banks have taken on, perhaps inadvertently, in an effort to boost revenue in an environment of lacklustre loan demand, low interest rates, excess liquidity and unprecedentedly narrow credit spreads," Yam said.   \par \par \uc2 Senior management and directors at banks around the world may lack expertise in understanding the market risks they are taking on when making sizeable investments in exotic instruments such as collateralised debt obligations. And there was a great need for robust stress-testing by banks, he said.   \par \par \uc2 Good credit ratings should not be taken as guarantees that an investment was risk-free, Yam said.   \par \par \uc2 "Recent developments have shown that the speed with which credit rating agencies react to changes in market environments leaves a lot of room for debate, and downgrades by them can have a pro-cyclical effect on market price, making life more difficult for those shouldering the risks," Yam wrote.   \par \par \uc2 HONGKONG/HKMA (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070906e396000lh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
