\par\par \b \uc2 U.S.'s Paulson highlights China environment efforts   \b0\par\par\uc2 By David Lawder   \par \uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 2007\par 13:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 QINGHAI LAKE, China, July 30 (Reuters) - U.S. Treasury Secretary Henry Paulson saw for himself on Monday efforts to reverse environmental degradation around China's largest inland lake, taking the spotlight off \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions for a day.   \par \par \uc2 "Climate change is a very important issue in this country, it's very important globally and it's very important in the U.S." Paulson told reporters during a visit to the Qinghai Lake, which is shrinking due to rising temperatures.   \par \par \uc2 "By coming here I call attention to what China is doing environmentally and reinforce what they're doing."   \par \par \uc2 Paulson, a longtime environmentalist who chaired The Nature Conservancy, said he was impressed with a programme funded by the central government to reclaim advancing desert areas near the lake by planting vegetation on sand dunes and former farmland.   \par \par \uc2 He said Qinghai Lake and glaciers on the Tibetan plateau were important for the global climate because shrinkage of the lake and melting of the glaciers could permanently shift the jetstream, bringing severe weather to other continents. Likewise, carbon emissions elsewhere could hasten the lake's demise.   \par \par \uc2 He said engagement on environmental issues was important to U.S. President George W. Bush, who wants to draw China into a coalition of the world's top carbon-emitting countries to formulate a plan for reducing greenhouse gas emissions.   \par \par \uc2 The tougher part of Paulson's China trip will follow in Beijing, where he will meet Vice Premier Wu Yi and \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Zhou Xiaochuan on Tuesday and President Hu Jintao on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 He said he would again press for faster appreciation of the yuan and other reforms, such as rebalancing China's economy away from exports and toward more domestic consumption and increasing foreign access to China's financial services sector.   \par \par \uc2 Paulson's visit comes as U.S. lawmakers, frustrated with slow progress in reducing U.S. trade deficits with China, are advancing legislation aimed at pressuring Beijing to allow open markets to set the yuan's value.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Senate Finance Committee last week passed a bill that would allow companies to seek anti-dumping duties against products from countries that have "fundamentally misaligned" \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and eventually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Federal Reserve.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Daily said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill smacks of strong protectionism and risks undermining bilateral efforts to reduce the trade imbalance between China and the United States.   \par \par \uc2 The measure would do little to cut the U.S. trade deficit, the English-language daily said in an editorial. The United States should concentrate instead on persuading its citizens to consume less and save more.   \par \par \uc2 "Unfortunately, the new U.S. bill tends to mislead its people into believing that protectionism can be an answer to its economic woes," the paper said.   \par \par \uc2 Paulson said he was concerned about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation, saying it was the wrong approach, and he preferred achieving \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and economic reform through bilateral and multilateral dialogue.   \par \par \uc2 But he understood the motivation behind it and frustrations among Americans about trade imbalances.   \par \par \uc2 "I don't want China to become an increasingly big political issue in the U.S.," he said.   \par \par \uc2 USA-CHINA/PAULSON (PICTURE)|LANGEN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|RNA|ABX|BNX|FUN|G|RBN|ABN|M|E|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|RNP|DNP|PGE|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070730e37u001ma\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
