\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-France's  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  push struggles to win wider G7 backing   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Swaha Pattanaik   \par \uc2 695 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2007\par 16:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  PARIS, July 23 (Reuters) - France is taking a lonely stance by complaining about \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  sinking to record lows against the euro, with fellow members of the G7 rich nations unwilling to pressure China or others with tactics they see as divisive.   \par \par \uc2  President Nicolas Sarkozy has made it his mission to complain about the export-damaging effects for France and the euro zone of what he has termed "monetary dumping" by other regions in the world.   \par \par \uc2  His oft-repeated list of countries that are using their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost growth lumps together Japan, the United States and China, with Beijing the focus of his most recent attacks.   \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the same day that China raised its interest rates to cool its economy, Sarkozy said the value of the yuan was a problem and that he wanted to discuss the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the Chinese authorities.   \par \par \uc2  While some in the Group of Seven may privately share his frustration at the pace at which the Chinese authorities are allowing the yuan to strengthen, there are few public backers for Sarkozy's drive.   \par \par \uc2  "China's steps are very small and we would like them to move faster but, the thing is, you do not force China to do what you want them to do," one European finance source told Reuters.   \par \par \uc2  "They have moved already. While it is not far enough in our eyes, they are at least moving and what you have to do is talk to them and convince them."   \par \par \uc2  COOL RECEPTION   \par \par \uc2  The yuan hit an intraday high of 7.5607 per dollar last week, its trading peak since Beijing revalued the yuan and depegged it from the dollar in July 2005.   \par \par \uc2  On Monday, dollar weakness took the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a record low of $1.3844 to the euro, a 26-year low against the British pound at $2.0603, and a six-week low of 120.82 yen, while the euro hit a record high versus the yen in mid July at 168.96 yen, according to Reuters data.   \par \par \uc2  Germany, France's traditional European Union ally, has kept its distance from Sarkozy's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  calls even though it has not rejected them as brutally as it did French suggestions of more dialogue between the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and politicians.   \par \par \uc2  Like other members of the G7, Germany has signed up to the joint calls on China to introduce more flexibility into its exchange rates. However, it remains firmly opposed to bashing Beijing in public over its exchange rate policy.   \par \par \uc2  Nor is there any support in Germany for coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign exchanges to curb euro strength against a range of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the dollar and the yen.   \par \par \uc2  Britain and the United States are also loath to consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on floating exchange rates -- not least because  both countries are firm believers in letting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets decide exchange rates.   \par \par \uc2  There is also some sympathy in both capitals for the view that exerting more public pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  could backfire.   \par \par \uc2  In past decades Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and it keeps saying that it is watching \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves carefully.   \par \par \uc2  However, Tokyo has stayed out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since 2004 and is sticking to the line that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be set by markets.   \par \par \uc2  Economic fundamentals are also militating against official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to analysts -- particularly Japan's low interest rates, which weaken the yen by encouraging investors to borrow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy higher yielding assets.   \par \par \uc2  What France can reasonably hope for is some slight modification in the language of the G7 statements that carries a hint of what it wants -- but even changes at this level could be minimal.   \par \par \uc2  "If there was an appetite (for stronger language on China) they would have done it already, so I would be surprised if the language hardened up too much," the European finance source said.  (With additional reporting by Yoko Nishikawa in Tokyo, Gernot Heller in Berlin, Sumeet Desai in London, Glenn Somerville in Washington)       \par \par \uc2 G7-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|J|Z|NAT|UKI|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070723e37n001rk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
