\par\par \b \uc2 US Sens Dodd,Shelby Introduce  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2 -Manipulation Bill   \b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2007\par 22:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--Leaders on the U.S. Senate Banking Committee on Thursday said they had introduced legislation aimed at toughening U.S. laws against \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market manipulation by trading partners.   \par \par \uc2 Committee Chairman Christopher Dodd, D-Conn., and ranking member Richard Shelby, R-Ala., last week announced their intention of introducing their version of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -manipulation bill. They are following colleagues on the Senate Finance Committee, who have offered their own legislation.   \par \par \uc2 The Dodd-Shelby bill would identify illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by a country to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a time when that country is running a global trade surplus, as well as a two-way trade surplus with the U.S. That definition now fits China.   \par \par \uc2 "Just last week, the Treasury Department admitted that there exists 'heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to manage the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,'" Dodd said in a statement. "Yet Treasury still refuses to officially identify China as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator, despite this evidence that the Chinese government is continuing to undervalue its exchange rate against the U.S. dollar."   \par \par \uc2 Currently, countries are in violation of U.S. trade laws when the Treasury Department determines \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is carried out with the intent of gaining trade advantage. Those countries must enter formal consultations with the U.S. to discuss the issue.   \par \par \uc2 Though under heavy pressure from Congress to penalize China, the Bush administration last week again said it can't prove the intent of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is to cheapen its exports.   \par \par \uc2 China manages the value of its yuan through a system of capital controls and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The government has said it plans to gradually increase flexibility of the yuan against the U.S. dollar, and has allowed appreciation of about 8.5% since it abandoned its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peg against the dollar in July 2005. That pace is too slow for the U.S. Congress and the Treasury Department, whose officials have repeatedly called on China to move faster.   \par \par \uc2 The Dodd-Shelby bill would require the U.S. to pursue consultations on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy at the International Monetary Fund and to file complaints at the World Trade Organization. -By Elizabeth Price, Dow Jones Newswires; 202-862-9295; Elizabeth.Price@dowjones.com [ 21-06-07 2008GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070621e36l000z1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
