\par\par \b \uc2 3RD UPDATE: China Once More Escapes Being Labeled A  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Manipulator   \b0\par\par\uc2 844 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2007\par 23:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 By Greg Robb   \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones) -- China's management of its dynamic, fast-growing economy leaves much to be desired, but the mainland has not met the technical requirements to be designated as a manipulator of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Treasury Department concluded Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 "China should not hesitate any longer to take far more vigorous action to rebalance its economy, promote immediate [yuan] movement to tackle the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's undervaluation, and achieve far greater flexibility in the exchange-rate regime," a Treasury report said.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts were not surprised by the decision against naming China as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator. They said that such a designation would be one step too far for the Bush administration, which is seeking Beijing's help to manage North Korea and other global hot spots.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said that had the Treasury called China a manipulator, it would it have given Congress a green light to pass legislation imposing tariffs on Chinese imports, potentially setting off a trade war.   \par \par \uc2 As it is, a bipartisan group of leaders of the Senate Finance Committee will unveil a China trade bill later Wednesday aimed at forcing China to allow its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen against the dollar. The measure rewrites the playbook for handling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation and sets out a timetable for remedial action.   \par \par \uc2 "We know that China can do more," said Sen. Charles Schumer, Democrat of New York, a leading critic of China's exchange rate regime.   \par \par \uc2 "This bill was made in China," said Sen. Lindsey Graham, Republican of South Carolina, another key backer of the bill.   \par \par \uc2 But backers of the legislation still have to negotiate with the White House and the House of Representatives to craft a bill, which may well have to be watered down to win approval.   \par \par \uc2 The bipartisan leaders of the Senate Banking Committee released a competing bill that tightens the definition of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation and removes a requirement that the government find the manipulation was intended to boost exports or foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 "Treasury talks tough, but at the end of the day their report is like milquetoast," said Sen. Richard Shelby, Republican of Alabama, and the ranking Republican on the Banking Committee in a television interview.   \par \par \uc2 Shelby said his bill would have a better definition of manipulation and push Treasury to work more closely on the issue with the International Monetary Fund.   \par \par \uc2 U.S. manufacturing and labor interests have said China's undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cost hundreds of thousands of jobs as cheap Chinese imports flood the market.   \par \par \uc2 Many economists say the difference is really that Chinese workers are paid far less than American workers and that strengthening the yuan will do little to address this gap.   \par \par \uc2 Chinese officials have said they have to go slow to strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There is concern that a higher \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could encourage speculators and hurt the economy.   \par \par \uc2 The Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shown cumulative appreciation of around 8.3% since Beijing revalued the yuan by 2.1% in July 2005.   \par \par \uc2 Going by its semiannual report, the Treasury seems most concerned that China's exchange-rate policy could create global difficulties.   \par \par \uc2 Heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan from rising has led to the accumulation of excessive reserves, estimated by Treasury at $1.066 trillion at the end of last year.   \par \par \uc2 All of this money sloshing around China's domestic economy increases the risk of overheating and asset bubbles, the report concluded. Inflation has already picked up in China recently.   \par \par \uc2 "These trends clearly increase the risk of a renewed boom-bust cycle, which would be quite harmful for the global economy," the report said.   \par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve officials seem to share the concern.   \par \par \uc2 In a speech in Singapore earlier Wednesday, Timothy Geithner, the president of the New York Fed, said there was a growing risk of inflation in Asia, in part from the buildup of reserves and the "policy conflict" at China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support a fixed exchange rate and stable inflation.   \par \par \uc2 "Although measured inflation in emerging Asian economies remains relatively low, the pace of credit growth and the behavior of asset prices provide some evidence of a growing tension among competing objectives," he said.   \par \par \uc2 "The longer this policy conflict persists, the greater the distortions building up in the economy, the greater the risk of future inflation and the greater the risk of a bumpy future," Geithner said.   \par \par \uc2 The report said that Treasury Secretary Henry Paulson forcefully raises the Chinese exchange-rate regime at every available opportunity.   \par \par \uc2 The report was not all negative. It said there were signs that imbalances that have threatened the global expansion have begun to ease a bit.   \par \par \uc2 In a separate announcement, U.S. Trade Representative Susan Schwab announced her agency has rejected another petition to initiate World Trade Organization dispute settlement procedures against China over that country's exchange rate policies.   \par \par \uc2 "We do not believe that this Section 301 petition is likely to be the most productive way to secure Chinese movement toward \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility," said Schwab. [ 06-13-07 1706ET ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020070613e36d0001f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
