\par\par \b \uc2 = US Tsy Declines To Designate China As  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Manipulator   \b0\par\par\uc2 760 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2007\par 16:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, Jun 13, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --   \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Elizabeth Price\par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 The Bush administration, in a decision sure to fire up critics on Capitol Hill, has again declined to name China or any other trade partner guilty of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation.   \par \par \uc2 In its latest semi-annual report to Congress on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies around the world, the U.S. Treasury Department said that China is moving too slowly to phase out heavy management of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , known as the yuan or the renminbi, but its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't meet the legal definition for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation under U.S. law.   \par \par \uc2 "Although the renminbi is undervalued and market sentiment clearly favors appreciation, Treasury concluded that China did not meet the technical requirements for designation," Treasury said. "Treasury was unable to determine that China's exchange rate policy was carried out for the purpose of preventing effective balance of payments adjustment or gaining unfair competitive advantage in international trade."   \par \par \uc2 China tightly manages its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through a system of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls and dollar purchases on international \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Treasury noted that during 2006, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped push up \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by $247.5 billion, to $1.066 trillion at the end of the year. Reserves continued to climb in the first quarter of this year to $1.2 trillion by the end of March.   \par \par \uc2 "Prolonged one-way \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an unprecedented amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve accumulation, and a rapidly increasing current account surplus are clear indicators of fundamental renminbi undervaluation," Treasury said. "While China has taken some steps to increase the flexibility of the renminbi, the pace of appreciation that the authorities have allowed is much too slow and should be quickened."   \par \par \uc2 Since China abandoned its peg in July 2005, the yuan has appreciated about 8.3% against the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The slow pace of reform has amplified \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tendency toward boom-bust cycles as the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has boosted money supply, lowering interest rates, which in turn encouraged more borrowing and investment, Treasury said. Though the government has stated a goal of more balanced growth, with a higher share of consumption, China's current policies and the rigid exchange rate contributed to more unbalanced growth last year, Treasury said.   \par \par \uc2 For more than two years, some members of Congress have threatened to enact new legislation making it easier to penalize China for preventing market forces from raising the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Senate Banking Committee leaders Tuesday said they would introduce a bill defining manipulation as prolonged one-way \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  combined with global and bilateral trade surpluses, leaving aside the question of intent. Other key senators on the Senate Finance Committee have said they plan to offer their version of a bill Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Treasury said the U.S. current account deficit, a broad measure of trade, appears to have peaked as growth slowed in the U.S. and picked up in Europe and Japan.   \par \par \uc2 "Growth in Europe and Japan has been well above recent five-year averages," Treasury said. "To rebalance global demand, Europe and Japan will need to implement further structural reforms and sustain and boost their respective paces of domestic demand growth."   \par \par \uc2 Treasury noted that Japan now maintains a freely floating exchange rate and hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since 2004. Recent weakness in the value of the Japanese yen versus the U.S. dollar reflects low interest rates in Japan, needed to safeguard economic recovery.   \par \par \uc2 "Japan's economic recovery continues, but it has not proved sufficiently robust for the Japanese economy to durably exit price deflation," Treasury said.   \par \par \uc2 Treasury also noted the rapid rise in the value of sovereign wealth funds, or government investment vehicles funded by \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets. The largest of these are oil funds, but in Asia countries with excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are transferring assets to stand-alone funds.   \par \par \uc2 Treasury said these funds are less transparent than \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which fall under reporting rules established by the International Monetary Fund. The mystery surrounding these funds leads to wide-ranging estimates for their value of between $1.5 trillion to $2.5 trillion, compared with about $5.1 trillion of official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves as of the end of January.   \par \par \uc2 Treasury pondered whether international best-practice guidelines need to be developed for managing these assets.   \par \par \uc2 -By Elizabeth Price, Dow Jones Newswires; 202-862-9295; Elizabeth.Price@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires   \par \par \uc2 06-13-07 1000ET   \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070613e36d0018w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
