\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market reopened after a weeklong holiday.   \par \par \uc2 The local dealer added the dollar may drop further this week, but expected strong support at CNY7.6400.   \par \par \uc2 A Shanghai-based dealer with a foreign bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have also moved to pull the yuan down earlier in the day by posting the dollar-yuan central parity at 7.6538, well above Monday's closing level.   \par \par \uc2 Offshore, the one-year dollar-yuan nondeliverable forwards were at 7.2724/7.2774, up from 7.2590/7.2640 late Monday afternoon.   \par \par \uc2 -By Denis McMahon, Dow Jones Newswires; 8621 6120-1200; denis.mcmahon@dowjones.com [ 29-05-07 0819GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1153   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070529e35t000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
