al dealer added the dollar may drop further this week, but expected strong support at CNY7.6400. A Shanghai-based dealer with a foreign bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have also moved to pull the yuan down earlier in the day by posting the dollar-yuan central parity at 7.6538, well above Monday''s closing level. Offshore, the one-year dollar-yuan nondeliverable forwards were at 7.2724/7.2774, up from 7.2590/7.2640 late Monday afternoon. -By Denis McMahon, Dow Jones Newswires; 8621 6120-1200; denis.mcmahon@dowjones.com -0-    \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020070529e35t004bl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
