\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ UPDATE:China's Zhou:Pace Of Yuan Exchange Rate Reform 'Good'   \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2007\par 02:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2007, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with Zhou quotes, background on talks)   \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--China''s \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said Wednesday he believes the pace of reform of the yuan exchange rate 'is good,' pointing out he also faces domestic pressure to slow the yuan''s rise in addition to U.S. pressure to accelerate it.   \par \par \uc2 'We agree on the general direction of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform,' People''s Bank of China Governor Zhou Xiaochuan told reporters after a meeting with members of the U.S. Congress in Washington. 'There''s probably a little bit of difference on how fast we should carry it out.'   \par \par \uc2 Members of the House Ways and Means Committee, in a letter to Chinese Vice Premier Wu Yi that was hand delivered to her at their meeting earlier Wednesday, said they have 'serious concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 ''s massive and constant \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.'   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has allowed its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate by around 8% versus the U.S. dollar, including a one-time 2.1% rise, since July 2005.   \par \par \uc2 Referring to the exchange of views with the members of the U.S. Congress, Zhou said: 'They may think that we can accelerate the speed of reform, but we think that we have already tried our best and domestically we have pressure to slow down a little bit.'   \par \par \uc2 Zhou said China''s government is under pressure from its own domestic exporters and other sectors to slow the pace of the yuan''s rise.   \par \par \uc2 China took a small step toward allowing greater flexibility in its exchange rate regime Friday when it increased the daily trading band on the yuan to 0.5% versus the dollar. Previously the trading band was 0.3% versus the dollar and had rarely come close to testing that limitation.   \par \par \uc2 A delegation of senior Chinese officials, led by the vice premier, is visiting Washington this week for the second round of the U.S.-China Strategic Economic Dialogue.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rick Carew, Dow Jones Newswires; 202-862-9295; Rick.Carew@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -0-    \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020070524e35o000gp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
