\par\par \b \uc2 China advised to learn from Chile on managing  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2007\par 05:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BEIJING, April 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  should learn from Chile how to scale back \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, a senior government economist said.   \par \par \uc2 Li Yang, a researcher with the Chinese Academy of Social Sciences, the government's top think-tank, said Chile's experience in reducing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and making its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  transparent marked a "successful combination of market-oriented mechanisms and appropriate government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".   \par \par \uc2 Whereas the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  (PBOC) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to control the yuan <CNY=CFXS>, he said Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had greatly reduced its presence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since it adopted a floating exchange rate regime in September 1999.   \par \par \uc2 Li, a former academic member with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy committee, was writing in the latest edition of China Finance, a bi-monthly journal affiliated with the PBOC.   \par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to Li, has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market only 15 times in the last six years to stabilise the Chilean peso <CLP=CL>.   \par \par \uc2 By contrast, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- to keep the yuan from rising too fast or to deter speculation -- would not help Beijing attain its goal of building up a market-oriented exchange rate system, he said.   \par \par \uc2 Beijing scrapped the yuan's peg to the dollar in July 2005 in favour of a managed float with reference to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the details of which are secret.   \par \par \uc2 Chinese officials, including PBOC Governor Zhou Xiaochuan, have pledged to let market forces eventually determine the yuan's exchange rate. However, for now, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still has the ultimate say setting the rate, economists say.   \par \par \uc2 CHINA-FINANCIAL/CHILE|LANGEN|Z|ABN|M|D|ABX|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070430e34u0004j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
