\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Weaker Vs EUR, JPY Ahead Of FOMC Decision  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Patrick Bennett  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 698 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 05:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The euro and the Japanese yen are firmer against an overall modestly weaker U.S. dollar Wednesday, with Asian trade curtailed by a Japanese holiday for Vernal Equinox Day and attention on the Federal Open Market Committee meeting later.  \par \par \uc2 At 0450 GMT, the dollar was trading at Y117.28, against Y117.80 at the same time Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was trading at $1.3315, against $1.3295 at the same time Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar is expected to remain in consolidation near term, but with the speculative market believed to be short of dollars against the yen after Tuesday's fall, the U.S. unit could rally to Y117.50 later as positions are covered ahead of the FOMC, according to a Singapore trader.  \par \par \uc2 Many analysts expect the Fed to concede the economic outlook has softened and that the housing market is less buoyant, though there is little expectation the Fed will completely extinguish its stand against inflation.  \par \par \uc2 "The FOMC statement is likely to acknowledge the deterioration in the economic outlook, even as the Fed will continue to take a relatively upbeat view."  \par \par \uc2 "We expect the Fed to retain its tightening bias, if only so as not to spark speculation of a near-term rate cut," said Jan Lambregts, Asian head of research at Rabobank.  \par \par \uc2 Traders say that given broad consensus on the outcome of the FOMC, a large move outside of recent ranges in the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs isn't likely.  \par \par \uc2 Key support for the dollar is at the March 14 low of Y115.76, and against the euro at the Dec. 4 low of $1.3367, Dow Jones technical analysis shows. Breaks beyond those levels would indicate potential for more significant dollar weakness in the days ahead.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell against the yen overnight Tuesday after China \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Zhou Xiaochuan reportedly said the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't "intend to go further and accumulate (foreign) reserves."  \par \par \uc2 But most analysts believe the comments were either misinterpreted, or at the very least, not reflective of the reality that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem appreciation pressures in the yuan.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar remains lower against the yen, but additional losses are not expected as a result of the Chinese statement.  \par \par \uc2 "We don't believe it has been an intention for China to accumulate \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in the manner that it has, but is rather the by-product of other policies. In that sense, the comments should not be construed as either positive or negative for the dollar," said UBS Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Ashley Davies.  \par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the Malaysian ringgit reached a nine-year high against the dollar earlier today following comment from Prime Minister Abdullah that he wants the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen.  \par \par \uc2 At 0450 GMT the dollar was trading at MYR3.4815, against MYR3.4995 at the same time Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EDT / 0450 GMT\par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \pa