\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won up to 1-mth high on China  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  report  \b0\par\par\uc2 537 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 01:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, March 21 (Reuters) - The South Korean won <KRW=> rose to a one-month high against the dollar on Wednesday as a report that China would stop stockpiling its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves prompted investors to clear dollar long positions.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also lifted by exporters' deals and after South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed fourth quarter economic growth in Asia's third-largest economy was slightly revised up.  \par \par \uc2 But the won slimmed earlier gains as major companies gear up to pay dividends to foreign shareholders and on caution over possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities.  \par \par \uc2 The won was last quoted at 938.1/8.6 per dollar, after hitting a session high of 936.2, the strongest since 936 on Feb. 21, compared to its previous closing bid of 941.4.  \par \par \uc2 "Offshore players seemed to adjust their positions not only on the news of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves but also on expectations for emerging market stabilisation," a local bank dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may gain further with a target of 935 despite wariness of the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 The Emerging Markets magazine quoted \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Zhou Xiaochuan as saying in an interview published on Tuesday that China would stop accumulating massive foreign reserves See [ID:nN20351191] for details.  \par \par \uc2 But a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  official at South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  played down any impact on the won, saying the People's Bank of China is unlikely to stop adding \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 South Korean investors showed concern that such a move could trigger dollar sales, as a major supporter of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  changes tack.  \par \par \uc2 The yen <JPY=> was at 117.51/54 per dollar versus 117.26/29 in late New York trade on Tuesday. Japanese financial markets are closed on Wednesday for a public holiday.  \par \par \uc2 On the local economic front, South Korea's economy expanded a seasonally adjusted 0.9 percent in the last three months of 2006 from the previous quarter, just above a 0.8 percent rise estimated previously, revised \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed. [ID:nSEV000036]  \par \par \uc2 The country's exports in the first 20 days of the month rose 16.2 percent to $16.83 billion from a year ago, with a deficit of $1.59 billion, according to the commerce ministry. The monthly trade data does not necessarily follow interim figures.  \par \par \uc2 Investors are keeping an eye on the results of a two-day monetary policy meeting of the Federal Reserve, which started on Tuesday at which the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen holding interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 On the Seoul stock market, foreign investors bought a net 43.9 billion won worth of shares with the main KOSPI index <.KS11> ending down 0.09 percent.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                     0725 GMT     0435 GMT  prev close\par  Won <KRW=>           938.1/8.6    937.3/8.0       941.4\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>  7.9784/860    7.9937/83      8.0263\par  KOSPI <.KS11>         1,442.85     1,440.26    1,444.17\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070324e33l0000s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
