\par\par \b \uc2 US Congress To Grill Tsy's Paulson On China  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Wed  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Elizabeth Price  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 671 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2007\par 00:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--U.S. Treasury Secretary Henry Paulson will face a much tougher audience in Congress Wednesday when he discusses his view on China's heavily managed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime.  \par \par \uc2 Paulson plans to testify before the Senate Banking Committee on the Treasury Department's most recent decision not to brand China guilty of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation in its semi-annual report to Congress. When the report was released in December, two months overdue, Senate Banking Committee Chairman Chris Dodd, D-Conn., said he was "deeply disappointed" with Treasury's position.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation may sound like a complicated financial issue but its impact on Americans is not -millions of American families have lost a job in the manufacturing sector over the past five years," Dodd said in a statement Monday. "The fact that the administration failed to find that China was engaged in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation in their most recent report is troubling, to say the least."  \par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  each month buys dollars on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to tightly control the value of the Chinese yuan. In July 2005, China officially ended its policy of pegging its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar and moved to managing the yuan against an unpublished basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The yuan appreciated 2.6% in 2005, and then another 3.4% in 2006.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan has been appreciating at a faster pace since last fall, with the government's central parity rate for the yuan regularly posting new highs. Most analysts predict the yuan will strengthen at least 4% to 5% against the dollar this year.  \par \par \uc2 However, that isn't enough for U.S. manufacturers and their representatives in Congress, who argue that China's rocketing trade surpluses and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves accumulation are evidence the yuan should be much stronger.  \par \par \uc2 Further, while the yuan has strengthened some against the U.S. dollar, it has done so at a time when the dollar mostly weakened against major trading partners. So, on a trade-weighted basis, the yuan has barely budged since the 2005 revaluation.  \par \par \uc2 In the December report, Treasury acknowledged the slow pace of yuan appreciation and the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves build-up - to over $1.0 trillion - propelled by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, it also said \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's actions don't meet the legal definition of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation with the intent of gaining trade advantage.  \par \par \uc2 The hearing this week is Paulson's first appearance before Congress since his confirmation hearings, when senators welcomed him to the job. At the time, Sen. Charles Schumer, D-N.Y., a member of the banking committee, praised Paulson effusively.  \par \par \uc2 "In the world of finance and international markets, there is simply no equal to Hank," Schumer said. "And at this critical point in our economy's history, he is the right man at the right place at the right time."  \par \par \uc2 Schumer, perhaps the most outspoken critic of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, attacked the December decision for relying on "technical and legalistic dodges."  \par \par \uc2 He, along with Republican Senator Lindsey Graham of South Carolina, has said he plans to team up with leaders of the Senate Finance Committee, of which he is also a member, to toughen laws dealing with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation and the required Treasury report on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 That could put Schumer, Graham, Dodd and other congressional leaders on a collision course with Paulson, who has spent a large portion of his time and energy at Treasury on intensified diplomacy with top-level officials on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and economic cooperation.  \par \par \uc2 Treasury released its latest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  report just days after Paulson led a delegation to China for the first meeting of a semi-annual gathering of cabinet-level officials from the U.S. and China. During the visit, Paulson said he believed "quiet diplomacy" is the most effective way to prod China to reform faster.  \par \par \uc2 -By Elizabeth Price, Dow Jones Newswires; 202-862-9295; Elizabeth.Price@dowjones.com [ 29-01-07 2318GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070129e31t0014k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
