\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan ends higher on late dollar selling  \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2007\par 11:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Jan 29 (Reuters) - China's yuan ended higher against the dollar on Monday, reversing early losses, helped largely by dollar sales in late afternoon trade, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan <CNY=CFXS> spent most of the day below Friday's close of 7.7758 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's mid-point at 7.7836 in the morning, down from Friday's 7.7817.  \par \par \uc2 "The yuan is consolidating after the recent strengthening," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a domestic bank said.  \par \par \uc2 However, last-minute dollar selling just before the market closed pushed up the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to finish at its intraday high of 7.7745.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan had closed stronger for three consecutive sessions until it began a short-term correction on Friday, which dealers said was sparked by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 It briefly hit 7.7680 on Thursday, the highest intra-day level since its July 2005 revaluation.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan has gained a further 4.3 percent against the dollar on top of the 2.1 percent revaluation that accompanied its depegging from the U.S. dollar in 2005.  \par \par \uc2 Market talk late last week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be raising interest rates had no visible impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, said the trader.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , seeking new ways to cope with the flood of funds pouring into China's money market, said on Monday it would begin to issue three-year bills regularly in its open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursdays.  \par \par \uc2 But traders said they did not view the new step as a tightening of monetary policy but a step that could help the bank reduce excess liquidity in the market.  \par \par \uc2 Before Friday's retreat, the yuan had risen 0.44 percent since the start of this year, or at an annual rate of 5 to 6 percent, spurring market expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would allow the yuan to rise at a faster pace this year after a 3.4 percent rise in 2006.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN-CLOSE|LANGEN|ABN|M|Z|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070129e31t000xb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
