\par\par \b \uc2 Daily Chinese yuan and money market update  \b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2007\par 11:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Jan 26 (Reuters) - Following is a summary of market activity and news articles on Friday relating to the yuan and China's money market.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par         DLR/CNY    EUR/CNY  YEN/CNY*  1-YR NDF**  1-YR VOLS**\par  Close     7.7758    10.0481   6.4006    7.5197   2.90/3.15pct\par  Mid-point 7.7817    10.0656   6.4010***\par  Pvs close 7.7705    10.0851   6.4464    7.5115   3.10/3.40pct\par Sources: <CNYX=CFXS>, <CNYNDF=>, <CNYVOL>\par  * Yuan per 100 yen.\par  ** Offshore NDF/VOLS figures as at 1010 GMT compared with\par levels at around the same time in the previous session.\par  *** The mid-point is a benchmark set by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The\par yuan may rise or fall 0.3 percent from its mid-point versus the\par dollar each day and 3.0 percent for non-dollar \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  MONEY AND BOND MARKET\par             7-day repo   90-day PBOC bill  1-yr treasury bond\par           <CN7DRP=CFXS>      <CN3MNFIX=R>        <CN1YTFIX=R>\par  Jan. 25           2.0645            2.5580              2.0845\par  Change on day   + 0.0578          + 0.0040            + 0.0009\par  Change on mth   - 0.2145          - 0.0870            - 0.0573\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Change in weighted average and percentage point(s).  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Please double-click on <CNFIXINDEX> for a full list of Chinese fixed-income reference rates.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKET NEWS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** Yuan weakens vs dlr on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 SHANGHAI - The yuan closed weaker against the dollar on Friday with dealers saying the People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in trading to curb the yuan's gains.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nSHA56962]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China bond yields continue to edge up on CPI  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SHANGHAI - China's money market and bond yields continued edging up in quiet trade on Friday after Thursday's higher-than-expected inflation data fuelled concern that an official interest rate hike could be imminent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nSHA136418]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China stocks mixed after policy fears fuel wild ride  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SHANGHAI - Chinese stocks ended mixed on Friday after swinging wildly in response to fears that the government viewed the market's bull run as excessive and had decided to cool it down.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nSHA171939]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLICY NEWS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** Senate panel eyes yuan mid-point at 7.7817/dlr  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WASHINGTON - The Senate Finance Committee will hold one or more hearings on China's exchange rate policy and other bilateral trade issues, possibly in "mid- to late March," a spokeswoman for the panel said on Thursday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nN25233081]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economy News  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** U.S. investor Rogers fuels concern on China stocks  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shanghai - Jim Rogers, a prominent U.S. fund manager, has fuelled concern about a bull run in China's stock market, analysts said, by suggesting in a TV interview this week that stocks may have become overvalued.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story: [ID:nSHA143870]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China sees falling petrochem prices in 2007-paper  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING - Prices for key petrochemical products are expected to fall in 2007 as demand weakens, continuing a downward trend from the end of last year on the back of world crude markets, an official paper reported on Friday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story:[ID:nPEK165032]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 To see a guide on contributions, please click on <CN/CONT1>.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|Table|Z|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070129e31q000xo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
