\par\par \b \uc2 Fed's Bernanke urges China to let yuan rise  \b0\par\par\uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2006\par 06:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BEIJING, Dec 15 (Reuters) - U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke said on Friday that Chinese policy-makers risk losing control of their economy unless they let their yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise in value and strengthen their financial system.  \par \par \uc2 "Monetary policy may be constrained by the lack of a reliable monetary transmission mechanism and by the relative inflexibility of the exchange rate, which inhibit the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to keep inflation low and to stabilize the economy," Bernanke said in remarks prepared for delivery to the Chinese Academy of Social Sciences in Beijing.  \par \par \uc2 "Further appreciation of the ... (yuan), combined with a wider trading band and with the ultimate goal of a market-determined exchange rate, would allow an effective and independent monetary policy and thereby help to enhance China's future growth and stability," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The Fed distributed a text of Bernanke's comments in Washington.  \par \par \uc2 Bernanke was in Beijing as part of a high-level U.S. delegation led by Treasury Secretary Henry Paulson. U.S. officials are trying to persuade China to work toward a freely floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which they believe could help lessen China's massive trade surplus with the United States.  \par \par \uc2 "Greater scope for market forces to determine the value of the RMB would also reduce an important distortion in the Chinese economy, namely, the effective subsidy that an undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  provides for Chinese firms that focus on exporting rather than producing for the domestic market," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Washington reported a record $24.4 billion trade deficit with China in October, 40 percent of the total U.S. trade deficit.  \par \par \uc2 As talks between U.S. and Chinese officials began on Thursday, China let the yuan hit its highest level since it revalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 2.1 percent in July 2005 and began to allow it to float within tightly managed bands.  \par \par \uc2 Bernanke urged accelerated reform of China's banking and financial system, saying that central banks can best steer monetary policy when investment and borrowing decisions are sensitive to interest rate rises or declines.  \par \par \uc2 "Monetary policy can work well only to the extent that financial markets are sufficiently developed to allow the monetary authorities' interest-rate decisions to affect economic activity in a reasonably predictable way," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Bernanke warned that China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will eventually run into problems if it continues to sell bonds to offset the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that are necessary to maintain the current close link of the yuan to the dollar -- a process called "sterilization."  \par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rate and the domestic interest rate is maintained at near its current level, incentives for capital inflows will remain in place, and the value of "sterilization" bonds will grow, interfering with the demand for other assets, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Also, perceptions that the yuan is undervalued could fuel additional capital inflows as investors bet on a rise in the yuan's value, he added. Speculative inflows would in turn increase the need for greater exchange market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond sales.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  also faces distortions in the allocation of capital from an undervalued exchange rate and an underdeveloped financial system, Bernanke said.  \par \par \uc2 "The principal imbalance lies in the composition of Chinese GDP (gross domestic product), which is heavily tilted toward investment and net exports and away from domestic consumption and government provision of social services," he said.  \par \par \uc2 CHINA-USA/BERNANKE (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|Z|G|RBN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|ABX|BNX|FUN|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061215e2cf000hq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
