\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Yuan volatility surges, may signal appreciation  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Fang Yan and Andrew Torchia  \par \uc2 811 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2006\par 10:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Aug 16 (Reuters) - Big swings in the dollar/yuan rate over the past three days suggest China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is becoming freer and more volatile -- and may presage faster appreciation of the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Since Monday, the yuan has moved more widely than at any time since it was revalued and depegged from the dollar in July 2005. On Tuesday, the yuan tumbled 0.28 percent, its biggest single-day percentage drop since the depegging.  \par \par \uc2 Those swings are only about half of what is allowed by the yuan's trading band, the edges of which are 0.3 percent on either side of a daily mid-point set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They don't approach the volatility of global markets, where daily moves of 1 percent are not uncommon.  \par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, long kept under tight control through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and moral suasion, is starting to look more developed in its capacity for sudden moves, short squeezes and general unpredictability.  \par \par \uc2 "Our \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is acting more like a 'normal' market now with those big swings," said Chen Gang, a trader at Shenzhen Development Bank. "This will make our jobs more exciting."  \par \par \uc2 Volatility began increasing several months ago, from a monthly average of 0.1 percent after the depegging to 0.2 percent in February 2006 and 0.3 percent in May, according to a study by BNP Paribas.  \par \par \uc2 Such volatility provides more lucrative trading opportunities for banks and should create a deeper market -- an avowed goal of Chinese authorities.  \par \par \uc2 But the swings also appear to have another goal, analysts said. They were largely in response to much weaker-than-expected yuan mid-points set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Some think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have engineered Tuesday's yuan tumble to punish speculators who it believes were betting excessively on appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 Many traders, however, subscribe to the opposite view -- that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is preparing for faster yuan appreciation by creating an environment in which large intra-day moves in both directions are common.  \par \par \uc2 TWO-WAY TRADE  \par \par \uc2 Since its revaluation, the yuan <CNY=CFXS> has appreciated slowly but steadily to a close of 8.0015 per dollar on Tuesday, a gain of 1.4 percent.  \par \par \uc2 This has entrenched a view there is little risk in betting on appreciation, meaning that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does allow a faster rise, the entire market is likely to come in on the side of the yuan every day. That would make it difficult for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to manage the appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 Qing Wang, Bank of America economist, said there was no doubt the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was effectively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it set its mid-points this week. "It's testing market acceptance for greater volatility, which could be two-way once the dollar loses steam."  \par \par \uc2 Chinese authorities are battling to restrain money supply growth, and yuan appreciation is one potential tool to achieve this, as a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  report noted this month.  \par \par \uc2 A survey of 10 local banks by Reuters last month found most expected a yuan rate of 7.70-7.90 around end-2006. That would represent appreciation of 1.3-3.9 percent, a faster pace than seen so far.  \par \par \uc2 It may not be a coincidence, traders said, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is introducing more volatility as China launches its Qualified Domestic Institutional Investor Programme, under which institutions will be allowed to invest Chinese clients' funds abroad.  \par \par \uc2 So far, institutions have won approval to invest up to $8.8 billion abroad. QDII-related outflows should help to create a two-way market by balancing some investment inflows.  \par \par \uc2 One way authorities could encourage more volatility would be to ease restrictions on trading practices, particularly a requirement that banks essentially square positions each day.  \par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, there have been rumours some Chinese banks have started to square only at the end of each week, perhaps with the tacit consent of authorities.  \par \par \uc2 Traders at local and foreign banks contacted by Reuters said they had no evidence this was happening. Officials at the State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade System said they were not aware of any rule changes.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said a relaxation of the squaring rule was inevitable and could conceivably occur this year if authorities felt Chinese banks were ready to assume the risk.  \par \par \uc2 "It just does not make sense to tolerate more volatility while tying traders' hands," said Wang. "Such rules will surely be scrapped sooner or later. It's not a matter of if, it's a matter of when."  \par \par \uc2 (With additional reporting by Kevin Yao in Beijing and Vidya Ranganathan in Singapore)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN-CHANGE (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|J|ABX|BNX|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|O|OIL|SI  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060819e28g0004i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
